# Forge Intelligence — configuration
#
# EVERYTHING HERE IS OPTIONAL. With no configuration at all the console runs
# every default layer on keyless public-domain feeds (USGS, NASA FIRMS/EONET,
# NOAA SWPC, GDACS, CelesTrak, Treasury OFAC, RDAP).
#
# Nothing below fabricates data when unset — the feature reports that it is not
# configured and the layer stays empty. That is deliberate: on an intelligence
# surface, a plausible-looking invented datum is worse than a blank one.

# ── Cache and rate limiting ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unset → in-process memory. Fine for one instance; set this to share the feed
# cache and rate-limit counters across replicas.
# REDIS_URL="redis://localhost:6379"

# ── AI analyst ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unset → the analyst reports unavailable.
# GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=""
# FI_ANALYST_MODEL="google/gemini-3.7-flash"   # or anthropic/… or openai/…

# ── Operator access for the gated RECON tools ───────────────────────────
# The exposure and breach tools reach third parties, so they require an
# operator. Unset → they answer 401 and no one can run them.
# Send: Authorization: Bearer <token>
# FI_OPERATOR_TOKEN=""
# FI_OPERATOR_EMAIL="operator@example.com"

# ── Third-party sources that need YOUR licence ──────────────────────────
# Host exposure lookups. Shodan's keyless InternetDB endpoint is licensed for
# NON-COMMERCIAL use only, so this app calls the licensed host API instead and
# needs your own key. Unset → 503.
# SHODAN_API_KEY=""
#
# Breach exposure. The provider requires a commercial licensing agreement and
# mandates attribution. Set to 1 only to attest that you hold one. Unset → 503.
# FI_BREACH_LICENSED=""
#
# CVE lookups work without a key; a key raises the limit from 5 to 50 req/30s.
# NVD_API_KEY=""
#
# Energy quotes in the status ticker. Free key from eia.gov/opendata.
# EIA_API_KEY=""
# FI_MARKETS_URL="http://localhost:3000/api/intelligence/markets"
#
# Coordinates on RECON IP lookups. Point at your own geo-IP service; "{ip}" is
# substituted per lookup. GeoLite2 requires visible attribution wherever it is
# displayed — see docs/data-sources.md.
# FI_GEOIP_URL="https://example.internal/geoip/{ip}"

# ── Active scanning — DELIBERATELY UNCONFIGURED ─────────────────────────
# Scanning third-party hosts without written authorisation is unlawful in most
# jurisdictions. Only point this at infrastructure you own or are contracted to
# test. See docs/operations.md.
# SCANNER_URL=""
# SCANNER_KEY=""                       # sent as a ?key= query parameter
# FI_SCANNER_DISABLED_TYPES="vuln"     # quick|ssl|headers|rdns|tech|vuln
